Subtask 2.5: Understanding Job Status and Troubleshooting

    Job status meanings:
        Successful: All tasks completed without errors
        Failed: One or more tasks failed
        Error: Job encountered a system error
        Canceled: Job was manually stopped
        Pending: Job is waiting to start
        Running: Job is currently executing

    Troubleshoot a failed job (simulation):
        Create a job template with an intentionally incorrect playbook name
        Launch the job and observe the failure
        Review error messages in the output
        Identify the root cause from the error logs

    Common troubleshooting steps:
        Verify inventory hosts are accessible
        Check credential permissions
        Validate playbook syntax
        Review project synchronization status
        Check system resources and connectivity

